[{"id":67791,"sender_id":13,"sender_full_name":"Tim_Porter","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f5067a77bfb4640f798f193b25d43eba?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/derivation.20on.20a.20group.20.28glitch.29/near/67791\">#1</a> On the page <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/derivation%20on%20a%20group\">derivation on a group</a>, the first line should read:\n[For convenience we assume below that is a <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>-module, it does not in general have to be abelian and it suffices to have it a <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>-group.]</p>\n<p>The two <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>s in this are not showing up and I cannot see why. I tried copying ‘<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>-module’ from further down the page where it does display correctly, but that does not help. It is probably something dumb e.g. the fact there are square brackets around everything, butI thought I would report it as a glitch.</p>\n<p>(Edit: I removed the square brackets and… yippee it works. They now display correctly.)</p>","timestamp":1525345991,"subject":"derivation on a group (glitch)","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":67793,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/derivation.20on.20a.20group.20.28glitch.29/near/67793\">#2</a> Perhaps this is because <code>[brackets](URL)</code> is the Markdown syntax for external links, so the parser was trying to interpret that as the text of a link and got confused?</p>","timestamp":1525363132,"subject":"derivation on a group (glitch)","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":67799,"sender_id":13,"sender_full_name":"Tim_Porter","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f5067a77bfb4640f798f193b25d43eba?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/derivation.20on.20a.20group.20.28glitch.29/near/67799\">#3</a> That is more or less what I had thought.</p>","timestamp":1525364573,"subject":"derivation on a group (glitch)","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]}]